type: software
title: "The least functional dependence at negative footrule: the lower boundary of the region of Chatterjee's rank correlation and Spearman's footrule"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. For every Spearman footrule value strictly between -1/2 and 0, the least possible population value of Chatterjee's rank correlation is determined, together with the unique copula that attains it and a dual certificate valid for all copulas; this completes the exact region of the pair begun by Rockel. For example xi + 2 psi >= -0.6042071 for every copula. The regions under radial symmetry and positive or negative quadrant dependence are also determined; for stochastically decreasing copulas the lower edge is the same curve and the upper edge xi <= -2 psi is stated as a conjecture."
